#. Diagram label
msgid "Broadcast the hold to siblings"
msgstr ""

#: processes/sdlc/saturation-meta-merge.bpmn:42
#. Diagram label
msgid "Build pipeline"
msgstr ""

#: processes/sdlc/saturation-meta-merge.bpmn:48
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Called by the merge manager watch when queued runs are 60+ minutes old and nothing has landed, or when the owner says the runners are full."
msgstr ""

#: processes/sdlc/saturation-meta-merge.bpmn:79
#. Diagram label
msgid "Cancel queued PR runs; build, push, merge"
msgstr ""

#: processes/sdlc/saturation-meta-merge.bpmn:68
#. Diagram label
msgid "Choose A, B, C or D"
msgstr ""

#: processes/sdlc/saturation-meta-merge.bpmn:62
#. Diagram label
msgid "Dry-run, then ask the owner naming every PR"
msgstr ""

#: processes/sdlc/saturation-meta-merge.bpmn:73
#. Diagram label
msgid "Go?"
msgstr ""

#: processes/sdlc/saturation-meta-merge.bpmn:111
#. Diagram label
msgid "Hold released, nothing merged"
msgstr ""

#: processes/sdlc/saturation-meta-merge.bpmn:57
#. Diagram label
msgid "Hold, and name the heads to merge"
msgstr ""

#: processes/sdlc/saturation-meta-merge.bpmn:26
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Holds the swarm, runs the dry run, asks the owner once naming every PR, cancels queued PR runs (never a started main run), builds and lands one meta-merge PR per repository with a merge commit, closes out the members, and reports main's verdict."
msgstr ""

#: processes/sdlc/saturation-meta-merge.bpmn:108
#. Diagram label
msgid "Landed and reported"
msgstr ""

#: processes/sdlc/saturation-meta-merge.bpmn:43
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Mechanical: runs main's checks after the meta-merge lands and reports green or red. Judges nothing a declaration has not decided."
msgstr ""

#: processes/sdlc/saturation-meta-merge.bpmn:25
#. Diagram label
msgid "Merge steward"
msgstr ""

#: processes/sdlc/saturation-meta-merge.bpmn:92
#. Diagram label
msgid "Merged?"
msgstr ""

#: processes/sdlc/saturation-meta-merge.bpmn:52
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Message every sibling that pushes to the repositories involved: what is about to land, and hold pushes, merges and run cancels until done. Ask the coordinator to pass it on to any thread that cannot be reached."
msgstr ""

#: processes/sdlc/saturation-meta-merge.bpmn:80
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Never cancel a main push run that has started. Build from fresh main with merge commits, skipping conflicts, .github/workflows/ and subscriptions/. Open one PR per repository, merge it with a merge commit, and comment on each member PR with the link."
msgstr ""

#: processes/sdlc/saturation-meta-merge.bpmn:120
#. Diagram label
msgid "No"
msgstr ""

#: processes/sdlc/saturation-meta-merge.bpmn:103
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "One message to the owner: what merged, main's verdict per repository, and any open decision. On red, the fix goes to main as its own PR."
msgstr ""

#: processes/sdlc/saturation-meta-merge.bpmn:69
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Only the owner's own tap or words approve the landing. A PR the card does not name gets no merge from it."
msgstr ""

#: processes/sdlc/saturation-meta-merge.bpmn:38
#. Diagram label
msgid "Owner"
msgstr ""

#: processes/sdlc/saturation-meta-merge.bpmn:19
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Owner, 2026-11-02 06:57Z, with the runners full: cancel everything queued, pause new work, consolidate all ready PRs on one meta-merge branch, skip CI and rendering, and merge it. Then: coordinate with the swarm siblings when this happens, and make it repeatable across repositories. First run 2026-11-02 07:03Z: cat-harness#956 (7 PRs), cat-harness-tools#1385 (4) and fhir-harness#274 (1). Skill saturation-meta-merge holds the steps and the safety rules. This process bypasses merge:guard on purpose, so the owner's card, the PR body and a comment on each member PR are the record."
msgstr ""

#: processes/sdlc/saturation-meta-merge.bpmn:85
#. Diagram label
msgid "Post done to every held sibling"
msgstr ""

#: processes/sdlc/saturation-meta-merge.bpmn:86
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Post done with what landed and what is still open, also when nothing was merged. A hold with no done is an outage."
msgstr ""

#: processes/sdlc/saturation-meta-merge.bpmn:102
#. Diagram label
msgid "Report what landed and main's verdict"
msgstr ""

#: processes/sdlc/saturation-meta-merge.bpmn:97
#. Diagram label
msgid "Run main's checks"
msgstr ""

#: processes/sdlc/saturation-meta-merge.bpmn:47
#. Diagram label
msgid "Runners saturated"
msgstr ""

#: processes/sdlc/saturation-meta-merge.bpmn:16
#. Diagram label
msgid "Saturation meta-merge: land the ready PRs when the runners are full"
msgstr ""

#: processes/sdlc/saturation-meta-merge.bpmn:21
#. Diagram label
msgid "Sibling session"
msgstr ""

#: processes/sdlc/saturation-meta-merge.bpmn:63
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Stack the PRs on a meta-merge branch without pushing. Then post the full question (include, leave out with the reason, merge method, per repository), followed by the card: A go, B also the red ones, C dry run only, D cancel."
msgstr ""

#: processes/sdlc/saturation-meta-merge.bpmn:39
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Taps the card in the thread that merges: go with green and pending, also the red ones, dry run only, or cancel. A PR the card does not name gets no merge from it."
msgstr ""

#: processes/sdlc/saturation-meta-merge.bpmn:98
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The merge starts main's checks. Until tools#1384, a closed PR's run can cancel them, so the steward re-runs a cancelled main run."
msgstr ""

#: processes/sdlc/saturation-meta-merge.bpmn:119
#. Diagram label
msgid "Yes"
msgstr ""
